    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8817\n\nSPONSOR: MARCELLINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the incorporation of the Cold Spring Harbor volun-\nteer and exempt firemen's benevolent association\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would authorize the formation of the Cold Spring Harbor\nVolunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, Incorporated.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 creates the not-for-profit corporation Cold Spring Harbor\nVolunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, Incorporated.\nSection 2 stipulates those persons eligible for membership in the asso-\nciation. Section 3 outlines the purposes of the association. Section 4\nstipulates the powers and duties of the association. Section 5 requires\nthat a meeting of the corporation be held not later than three months\nafter the effective date of this act. Section 6 stipulates the control\nand disposal of association funds and property, the management and\ncontrol of its affairs and spells out the composition of the board of\ntrustees. Section 7 permits the association to collect taxes for the use\nand benefit of the member of the fire department e.g., the care, relief\nand assistance of sick, disabled, or indigent volunteer and exempt fire-\nfighters and their families.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVolunteer firefighters perform dangerous duties each and every day in\nour communities. They offer affordable, reliable protection to our\nhealth, well-being, and property. They receive no compensation for their\nefforts except our heartfelt thanks and a small \"pension\" benefit after\nyears of service.\n\nBy adopting this legislation, the Cold Spring Harbor Volunteer Fire\nDepartment, Inc. would be authorized to create a benevolent association\nwhich would be able to collect funds to be used for the benefit of fire-\nfighters who are sick, disabled or indigent or may have been injured or\nkilled in the line of duty or their families.\n\nAn analysis of the Special Acts of the 51 benevolent associations in\nNassau County, NY, reveals that 46 permit the expenditure of 2% tax\nfunds, for amongst other things, the care, relief or assistance of sick\nor disabled or indigent firemen and their families. The numbers are\nsimilar for Suffolk County, NY.\n\nThe Cold Spring Harbor Exempt Volunteer Fireman's Association, Inc.\ndesires only that which the vast majority (over 88%) of the benevolent\nassociations in Nassau and Suffolk Counties have -to provide aid, care,\nassistance for sick, disabled and indigent firemen and their families.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\nprovision of section 7 of this act shall apply to taxes due on premiums\nreceived on and after the effective date of this act.\n",
